00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:32,430
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:44,858 --> 00:00:46,526
I've decided not to enter the competition.

3
00:00:48,153 --> 00:00:49,112
What?

4
00:00:49,195 --> 00:00:50,196
You're not…

5
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:52,532
doing what?

6
00:00:52,615 --> 00:00:53,825
The competition.

7
00:00:53,908 --> 00:00:55,201
I'm not entering.

8
00:00:59,247 --> 00:01:00,373
I'm leaving.

9
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:05,503
Are you crazy?

10
00:01:05,587 --> 00:01:06,880
Have you lost your mind?

11
00:01:06,963 --> 00:01:08,590
How can you do music without competing?

12
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:11,384
Why do you think
there's no soul in my music?

13
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:13,845
"Soul"?

14
00:01:14,512 --> 00:01:15,638
Ever since I was little,

15
00:01:16,681 --> 00:01:18,099
I've been a competition machine.

16
00:01:18,683 --> 00:01:20,852
I've played with textbook precision,

17
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:24,856
and thanks to that, I've swept
all the competitions I've entered.

18
00:01:24,939 --> 00:01:26,399
But because of that,

19
00:01:28,067 --> 00:01:29,903
people say my music has no soul.

20
00:01:30,653 --> 00:01:31,863
The bigger problem is

21
00:01:32,697 --> 00:01:35,158
that I don't know how
to put soul into music or why…

22
00:01:38,411 --> 00:01:40,788
Or why it's missing in the first place.

23
00:01:41,372 --> 00:01:43,458
You say I just need to
place in the competition.

24
00:01:44,125 --> 00:01:46,085
What scares me is what comes after.

25
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:48,630
That's your reason?

26
00:01:49,464 --> 00:01:52,842
You want to ruin your career
over some pipe dream?

27
00:01:52,926 --> 00:01:55,220
Stop whining over nothing

28
00:01:55,887 --> 00:01:57,764
and just focus on the competition.

29
00:02:00,183 --> 00:02:01,184
Mom.

30
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:05,605
Why did you make me do music?

31
00:02:07,815 --> 00:02:09,150
What are you trying to say?

32
00:02:11,069 --> 00:02:12,278
You didn't want to play,

33
00:02:12,362 --> 00:02:14,280
but I forced you to do it.

34
00:02:14,364 --> 00:02:15,490
Is that it?

35
00:02:16,741 --> 00:02:17,867
Fine, then quit!

36
00:02:17,951 --> 00:02:19,577
If you want to blame me,

37
00:02:20,536 --> 00:02:21,579
just quit right now.

38
00:02:22,163 --> 00:02:23,873
If you won't enter the competition,

39
00:02:23,957 --> 00:02:26,209
then to hell with lessons and school!

40
00:02:28,586 --> 00:02:29,587
Okay.

41
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:31,422
I will.

42
00:02:32,715 --> 00:02:33,716
If that's what you want.

43
00:02:43,434 --> 00:02:48,356
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

44
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,733
EPISODE 4

45
00:03:07,583 --> 00:03:08,751
Really?

46
00:03:32,483 --> 00:03:33,860
This is so good.

47
00:03:50,918 --> 00:03:52,211
What's the meaning of this?

48
00:03:53,129 --> 00:03:54,130
I'm sorry.

49
00:03:55,006 --> 00:03:57,258
But I brought you news
you'll be very happy to hear.

50
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:03,139
Pi-o just announced
he won't enter any competitions.

51
00:04:04,182 --> 00:04:05,558
That was your wish, right?

52
00:04:06,517 --> 00:04:07,685
Pi-o quitting music, that is.

53
00:04:09,562 --> 00:04:10,521
He made the right choice.

54
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:15,860
It's a hundred times better to quit now

55
00:04:15,943 --> 00:04:17,904
than to struggle for nothing
and waste time.

56
00:04:19,238 --> 00:04:20,907
He's played music all his life.

57
00:04:21,783 --> 00:04:25,286
He cut back on sleep to practice
just to earn your approval.

58
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:28,498
He's about to ruin his career,
and that's all you can say?

59
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,833
Why do you hate Pi-o so much?

60
00:04:30,917 --> 00:04:32,418
Why?

61
00:04:35,171 --> 00:04:36,089
Why?

62
00:04:38,007 --> 00:04:41,427
Do you feel guilty
because he reminds you of Mother?

63
00:04:42,136 --> 00:04:43,429
Get the facts straight.

64
00:04:45,056 --> 00:04:47,642
You're the one
who broke your parents' hearts.

65
00:04:48,851 --> 00:04:51,020
You went overseas to become a ballerina,

66
00:04:51,104 --> 00:04:53,648
only to quit and come back
with a baby inside you.

67
00:04:54,357 --> 00:04:58,236
What father would accept a child
who ruined his daughter's life?

68
00:04:58,861 --> 00:05:00,822
And whose fault is it that I lost my way?

69
00:05:01,572 --> 00:05:02,907
It's all because

70
00:05:02,990 --> 00:05:05,952
you left your cancer-stricken wife
to cheat with a ridiculously young girl!

71
00:05:08,955 --> 00:05:11,290
Please calm down, Mr. Kang.

72
00:05:11,999 --> 00:05:12,834
You can't.

73
00:05:18,548 --> 00:05:20,383
You're so lucky, Seon-ju.

74
00:05:21,426 --> 00:05:24,303
You have a husband who loves you so much.

75
00:05:25,388 --> 00:05:27,432
I'm so jealous I could scream!

76
00:05:29,976 --> 00:05:32,562
But remember this.

77
00:05:32,645 --> 00:05:33,479
My mom…

78
00:05:35,398 --> 00:05:38,401
cursed you until the day she died.

79
00:05:39,068 --> 00:05:43,531
I'm going to watch with my own eyes

80
00:05:44,824 --> 00:05:47,118
to see if that curse actually comes true.

81
00:05:58,546 --> 00:05:59,964
You handled it well.

82
00:06:01,549 --> 00:06:02,633
You did well.

83
00:06:12,935 --> 00:06:14,020
So?

84
00:06:14,687 --> 00:06:16,189
What do we do now?

85
00:06:26,073 --> 00:06:27,116
What is this place?

86
00:06:27,867 --> 00:06:29,076
This is new to me.

87
00:06:30,328 --> 00:06:31,871
Choose any sheet music you need.

88
00:06:31,954 --> 00:06:33,164
Go with Lemieux for Beethoven,

89
00:06:33,247 --> 00:06:35,124
Nordgrave and Albreon for Chopin,

90
00:06:35,708 --> 00:06:37,710
and Gravenholt for Russian composers.

91
00:06:40,588 --> 00:06:42,590
You download all your sheet music, right?

92
00:06:42,673 --> 00:06:44,008
That's not bad,

93
00:06:44,675 --> 00:06:47,637
but sheet music differs
depending on the editor.

94
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,472
And musical research keeps evolving,

95
00:06:49,972 --> 00:06:53,100
so it's important to see for yourself
and choose what works for you.

96
00:06:55,186 --> 00:06:56,562
By the way, I've been thinking.

97
00:06:57,855 --> 00:07:00,733
Why don't we play
each other's accompaniments?

98
00:07:00,816 --> 00:07:03,361
It's not easy practicing together
without a goal,

99
00:07:04,028 --> 00:07:07,281
and it's hard to practice
a concerto alone.

100
00:07:12,995 --> 00:07:15,081
Why? You don't like the idea?

101
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:16,749
It's not that.

102
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:19,502
I think it's a great idea.

103
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:22,797
All right then.

104
00:07:23,798 --> 00:07:24,966
Rachmaninoff,

105
00:07:26,634 --> 00:07:27,885
Beethoven,

106
00:07:28,886 --> 00:07:30,805
and Tchaikovsky are a must.

107
00:07:31,764 --> 00:07:33,474
And we need to study the full score…

108
00:07:35,351 --> 00:07:36,602
So let's get this…

109
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:39,480
and this too.

110
00:07:40,898 --> 00:07:43,150
You need to know what I'm studying,

111
00:07:43,234 --> 00:07:44,527
so I'll buy yours too.

112
00:07:47,446 --> 00:07:48,281
Let's see.

113
00:07:49,156 --> 00:07:50,741
Why are you treating me so well?

114
00:07:51,617 --> 00:07:52,535
You're making me giddy.

115
00:07:53,744 --> 00:07:54,912
Don't get the wrong idea.

116
00:07:55,538 --> 00:07:58,291
I'm just covering all the bases
so my partner won't mess things up.

117
00:08:01,752 --> 00:08:04,714
What's with the sudden urge
to just enjoy playing?

118
00:08:06,841 --> 00:08:07,758
I just…

119
00:08:08,509 --> 00:08:09,885
I don't think

120
00:08:11,012 --> 00:08:13,097
I've ever played the piano
because it was fun.

121
00:08:15,683 --> 00:08:17,184
The first time

122
00:08:18,561 --> 00:08:21,480
music felt beautiful to me
was when I was five.

123
00:08:23,232 --> 00:08:25,192
I heard the second movement
of the Emperor Concerto

124
00:08:25,276 --> 00:08:27,028
coming from my grandfather's study.

125
00:08:27,945 --> 00:08:29,196
Even as a kid,

126
00:08:30,156 --> 00:08:32,575
I was totally blown away and wondered,

127
00:08:33,659 --> 00:08:35,161
"How can music be this beautiful?"

128
00:08:36,454 --> 00:08:37,747
That's when I thought,

129
00:08:38,956 --> 00:08:42,543
"I never knew music
could be so beautiful."

130
00:08:43,419 --> 00:08:47,256
"I never knew the piano
was such a beautiful instrument."

131
00:08:50,217 --> 00:08:51,886
"I want to play like that."

132
00:08:51,969 --> 00:08:53,638
"I want to become a pianist."

133
00:08:56,849 --> 00:08:58,809
Looking back,

134
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:03,731
I just wanted to play the piano
simply because I loved music.

135
00:09:08,736 --> 00:09:09,695
By the way…

136
00:09:13,032 --> 00:09:15,493
Why did Maestro Kang want to see you?

137
00:09:16,535 --> 00:09:17,578
What?

138
00:09:18,204 --> 00:09:19,121
The truth is,

139
00:09:20,456 --> 00:09:21,874
he's my grandfather.

140
00:09:23,626 --> 00:09:24,543
Oh, I see.

141
00:09:25,294 --> 00:09:26,587
He's your grandfather.

142
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:29,590
He was just being encouraging, I guess.

143
00:09:30,591 --> 00:09:32,009
We shook hands, and that was it.

144
00:09:32,093 --> 00:09:34,512
I thought he was going to
give me spending money.

145
00:09:40,476 --> 00:09:42,019
Hey, let's go.

146
00:09:42,103 --> 00:09:44,146
I'll show you a fun way to play the piano.

147
00:09:45,606 --> 00:09:46,774
Where are we going?

148
00:09:46,857 --> 00:09:48,734
Just hurry up and follow me!

149
00:09:55,241 --> 00:09:56,492
HADAM-DONG INSTRUMENTS

150
00:09:58,869 --> 00:10:00,913
-Take the one in the corner.
-Thank you.

151
00:10:00,996 --> 00:10:01,831
Come in!

152
00:10:10,798 --> 00:10:11,757
What are you doing?

153
00:10:44,582 --> 00:10:46,584
Relax, I just tweaked the inner voices.

154
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:47,793
Take a seat.

155
00:10:47,877 --> 00:10:49,044
Give it a try.

156
00:10:49,962 --> 00:10:51,172
Me?

157
00:10:51,255 --> 00:10:52,757
I don't know much about jazz.

158
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,717
No one knows everything from the start.

159
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,843
Just relax

160
00:10:56,343 --> 00:10:58,095
and let your hands go with the flow.

161
00:10:58,888 --> 00:11:00,306
Put that down. There.

162
00:11:20,534 --> 00:11:22,203
Hey, you're good.

163
00:11:26,415 --> 00:11:29,001
Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star
is in C major, so use C and…

164
00:11:29,084 --> 00:11:32,338
C MAJOR: A MAJOR KEY WITH C AS ITS TONIC
ALONG WITH ITS CORRESPONDING SCALE

165
00:11:34,048 --> 00:11:36,759
Tweak it a bit like this,
and it's a blues scale.

166
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,720
-Sounds more jazzy, right?
-Yeah.

167
00:11:40,304 --> 00:11:41,138
Give it a try.

168
00:11:41,222 --> 00:11:43,390
BLUES SCALE: A SCALE MADE BY ADDING
SPECIAL BLUES NOTES BETWEEN BASIC NOTES

169
00:11:49,063 --> 00:11:50,523
Are you a genius, sir?

170
00:11:52,483 --> 00:11:55,402
Just play whatever you feel in your heart.

171
00:11:55,486 --> 00:11:56,821
Don't worry about the rules,

172
00:11:57,404 --> 00:11:59,490
and trust yourself, okay?

173
00:12:38,028 --> 00:12:39,280
Thank you, sir!

174
00:12:39,864 --> 00:12:40,865
You got us where we are.

175
00:12:44,577 --> 00:12:46,871
All right, get home safely.

176
00:12:47,538 --> 00:12:48,664
See you tomorrow at practice.

177
00:12:48,747 --> 00:12:50,207
Okay, see you tomorrow.

178
00:12:52,918 --> 00:12:54,169
-Take care.
-You too.

179
00:13:03,387 --> 00:13:05,180
I was about to freeze to death.

180
00:13:08,475 --> 00:13:09,310
Jeez.

181
00:13:10,895 --> 00:13:14,523
Where the hell have you been
all night in this cold?

182
00:13:16,108 --> 00:13:17,401
That's the kid from before.

183
00:13:19,445 --> 00:13:22,031
Call him over here so I can see his face.

184
00:13:22,615 --> 00:13:23,699
He's dead meat too.

185
00:13:27,661 --> 00:13:29,538
What? You don't want to?

186
00:13:30,122 --> 00:13:31,206
Because he's your friend?

187
00:13:32,249 --> 00:13:33,792
Well, aren't you so cool?

188
00:13:35,336 --> 00:13:36,629
I'm sorry, Mr. Kim.

189
00:13:38,255 --> 00:13:40,466
I'll find a way to pay you back.

190
00:13:41,216 --> 00:13:42,593
How will you do that?

191
00:13:43,928 --> 00:13:44,845
Look at his shoes.

192
00:13:46,013 --> 00:13:47,598
His family must be rich.

193
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:50,893
Give me his number.

194
00:13:51,894 --> 00:13:52,853
Why?

195
00:13:52,937 --> 00:13:54,772
Because I said so. Give it to me!

196
00:13:54,855 --> 00:13:56,482
It's cold, and I want to go home.

197
00:13:57,274 --> 00:13:59,109
I'm trying to help you, kid.

198
00:14:01,487 --> 00:14:04,323
Sir, he has nothing to do with this.

199
00:14:04,907 --> 00:14:06,659
Let's not complicate things…

200
00:14:12,581 --> 00:14:13,540
Don't lecture me.

201
00:14:15,334 --> 00:14:16,418
You little punk.

202
00:14:17,419 --> 00:14:18,504
Am I a joke to you?

203
00:14:22,675 --> 00:14:24,134
No, don't!

204
00:14:24,218 --> 00:14:25,469
Come on!

205
00:14:26,512 --> 00:14:27,596
I said don't!

206
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,014
KANG PI-O
MOBILE

207
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:34,979
When I call you from now on,

208
00:14:35,521 --> 00:14:37,523
you'd better answer before the third ring.

209
00:14:42,528 --> 00:14:44,613
If you don't, I swear I'll kill you.

210
00:14:45,531 --> 00:14:47,282
Damn, it's cold.

211
00:15:13,892 --> 00:15:14,935
That's the kid from before.

212
00:15:16,353 --> 00:15:18,230
Call him over here so I can see his face.

213
00:15:18,814 --> 00:15:19,940
He's dead meat too.

214
00:15:37,082 --> 00:15:38,375
Where were you yesterday?

215
00:15:40,461 --> 00:15:41,754
You don't need to know.

216
00:15:42,337 --> 00:15:43,505
Why didn't you practice?

217
00:15:44,173 --> 00:15:46,967
You can lose your touch
if you skip even one day.

218
00:15:49,636 --> 00:15:51,680
Are you seriously going to quit piano?

219
00:15:54,892 --> 00:15:55,976
Hand over your credit card.

220
00:15:59,563 --> 00:16:02,858
I'm not spending money on a brat
who won't listen, so hand it over.

221
00:16:12,284 --> 00:16:13,952
And don't come home.

222
00:16:14,953 --> 00:16:16,538
If you're going to live like that,

223
00:16:17,664 --> 00:16:18,665
get out of this house.

224
00:16:23,921 --> 00:16:25,255
Are you kidding me?

225
00:16:36,266 --> 00:16:37,184
Shoot.

226
00:16:51,365 --> 00:16:52,324
Damn it.

227
00:16:54,409 --> 00:16:55,452
Hey, what's up?

228
00:16:55,536 --> 00:16:57,579
Where are you? Why are you whispering?

229
00:16:57,663 --> 00:16:58,956
I'm in the library.

230
00:17:00,082 --> 00:17:01,834
Let's meet up. Stay right there.

231
00:17:03,627 --> 00:17:04,837
Damn it.

232
00:17:32,447 --> 00:17:33,490
Choi Jeong-yo.

233
00:17:36,243 --> 00:17:37,202
Hey, you're here.

234
00:17:37,286 --> 00:17:38,829
Why are you sweating so much?

235
00:17:38,912 --> 00:17:39,830
Are you sick?

236
00:17:41,039 --> 00:17:42,749
No, it's just hot in here.

237
00:17:45,252 --> 00:17:47,296
Can I talk to you outside?

238
00:17:47,796 --> 00:17:48,630
Okay.

239
00:17:50,424 --> 00:17:53,302
HER SUSPICIOUS DOUBLE LIFE

240
00:17:55,888 --> 00:17:57,139
What is it?

241
00:17:59,433 --> 00:18:00,434
Can I…

242
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,854
stay in your dorm for a few days?

243
00:18:04,354 --> 00:18:05,606
-Huh?
-What is it?

244
00:18:05,689 --> 00:18:07,107
Do you feel uncomfortable?

245
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:08,650
No, it's not that.

246
00:18:10,485 --> 00:18:12,321
Why all of a sudden?

247
00:18:13,822 --> 00:18:15,866
If you feel uncomfortable, forget it.

248
00:18:15,949 --> 00:18:17,784
Uncomfortable? Of course not.

249
00:18:17,868 --> 00:18:19,745
Stay for as long as you want.

250
00:18:20,579 --> 00:18:21,413
Really?

251
00:18:29,796 --> 00:18:31,423
Hey, this way.

252
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:37,804
Come on!

253
00:18:58,575 --> 00:18:59,952
We almost got caught.

254
00:19:12,589 --> 00:19:13,423
Oh, sorry.

255
00:19:13,507 --> 00:19:16,093
I'm usually pretty good about cleaning up,

256
00:19:16,176 --> 00:19:17,469
but I woke up too early today.

257
00:19:26,228 --> 00:19:27,813
Make yourself at home.

258
00:19:28,855 --> 00:19:32,109
Hey, do you want to change into this?

259
00:19:34,111 --> 00:19:34,945
No thanks.

260
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:36,405
Okay.

261
00:19:38,031 --> 00:19:39,950
It's smaller than I thought.

262
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:42,494
You think so too, right?

263
00:19:43,495 --> 00:19:47,040
Do you want the bed?
I'll sleep on the floor.

264
00:19:53,839 --> 00:19:54,673
Oh jeez.

265
00:19:55,299 --> 00:19:56,550
Why is this here?

266
00:19:56,633 --> 00:19:57,759
Why is it…

267
00:19:59,011 --> 00:20:00,679
I'll just sleep on the floor.

268
00:20:00,762 --> 00:20:02,514
That's probably for the best.

269
00:20:20,365 --> 00:20:21,491
Hey, what is it?

270
00:20:22,701 --> 00:20:23,618
Hyun-soo.

271
00:20:26,705 --> 00:20:29,374
Am I really a harsh and overbearing mom?

272
00:20:32,210 --> 00:20:33,086
No.

273
00:20:33,879 --> 00:20:34,963
I don't see you that way.

274
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:39,468
It's okay.

275
00:20:41,678 --> 00:20:43,638
I know people talk behind my back.

276
00:20:45,474 --> 00:20:47,142
Those people

277
00:20:47,225 --> 00:20:50,520
didn't like me
even before I acted this way.

278
00:20:51,688 --> 00:20:52,939
So I didn't care.

279
00:20:55,025 --> 00:20:58,445
I couldn't care less
what those people said about me…

280
00:21:01,156 --> 00:21:03,283
because Pi-o was my priority.

281
00:21:06,661 --> 00:21:08,747
It was fine when they said it,

282
00:21:09,456 --> 00:21:10,624
but hearing Pi-o say it…

283
00:21:15,003 --> 00:21:16,338
My heart hurts

284
00:21:17,798 --> 00:21:19,216
as if it's being torn apart.

285
00:21:24,888 --> 00:21:27,474
Did I really do something so terrible?

286
00:21:32,104 --> 00:21:34,856
So why aren't you going home?

287
00:21:35,482 --> 00:21:36,900
Because you said no to competitions?

288
00:21:37,484 --> 00:21:38,318
Yeah.

289
00:21:39,528 --> 00:21:40,779
I knew what to expect…

290
00:21:43,698 --> 00:21:44,991
but it's still not easy.

291
00:21:46,618 --> 00:21:49,162
Still, I'm never going back
to how things were.

292
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:55,127
Oh, don't worry.

293
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:56,878
I won't stay long.

294
00:21:57,546 --> 00:21:58,505
What?

295
00:21:59,005 --> 00:22:01,758
No, that's not what I meant.

296
00:22:05,220 --> 00:22:06,179
I'm tired.

297
00:22:07,597 --> 00:22:08,640
I'm going to sleep.

298
00:22:10,642 --> 00:22:12,352
Okay. Good night.

299
00:22:31,163 --> 00:22:33,123
MR. KIM

300
00:22:33,206 --> 00:22:34,666
This is your friend's house, right?

301
00:22:34,749 --> 00:22:36,668
Wow, they're super rich.

302
00:23:02,444 --> 00:23:03,570
Where are you?

303
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,280
THE CONVENIENCE STORE

304
00:23:29,221 --> 00:23:31,348
-Hey.
-Hey, you're awake.

305
00:23:32,057 --> 00:23:32,974
What's this?

306
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,768
Do you compose too?

307
00:23:35,352 --> 00:23:36,520
No.

308
00:23:36,603 --> 00:23:39,022
I just scribbled whatever came to mind.

309
00:23:40,023 --> 00:23:41,691
Here, eat this.

310
00:23:41,775 --> 00:23:44,694
Why did you pick up food
when we could've gone out together?

311
00:23:44,778 --> 00:23:47,906
I just felt like taking a walk.

312
00:24:09,094 --> 00:24:09,970
Hold on.

313
00:24:12,722 --> 00:24:14,683
Do you know the meaning of concerto?

314
00:24:14,766 --> 00:24:15,892
Concerto?

315
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:19,563
No.

316
00:24:19,646 --> 00:24:21,648
It means "to fight" in Latin.

317
00:24:22,482 --> 00:24:25,402
Then it evolved to mean
"work together" in Italian.

318
00:24:26,111 --> 00:24:27,821
So in a concerto,

319
00:24:27,904 --> 00:24:31,241
a pianist has to fight and win
against a hundred orchestra members,

320
00:24:31,825 --> 00:24:33,827
while still working together at times.

321
00:24:33,910 --> 00:24:36,871
But your sound is trapped inside here.

322
00:24:39,332 --> 00:24:40,166
Wait.

323
00:24:43,962 --> 00:24:47,841
Imagine you're throwing the sound
toward me as you play.

324
00:24:47,924 --> 00:24:48,883
Throw the sound?

325
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:06,026
Exactly. That's much better than before.

326
00:25:07,611 --> 00:25:09,195
Keep practicing. I'll be right back.

327
00:25:14,576 --> 00:25:15,410
Throw the sound.

328
00:26:02,874 --> 00:26:05,460
Sorry. Should I start over?

329
00:26:05,543 --> 00:26:06,670
What was that just now?

330
00:26:07,462 --> 00:26:10,590
I heard the bell ring
and arranged it in Baroque style.

331
00:26:11,508 --> 00:26:13,009
Let's practice. Sorry.

332
00:26:24,229 --> 00:26:25,063
A.

333
00:26:29,234 --> 00:26:30,110
B flat.

334
00:26:32,112 --> 00:26:33,029
F sharp.

335
00:26:35,740 --> 00:26:36,658
G.

336
00:26:38,743 --> 00:26:40,161
Now improvise.

337
00:27:01,558 --> 00:27:02,600
Never mind.

338
00:27:03,768 --> 00:27:05,311
Just get warmed up.

339
00:27:50,064 --> 00:27:51,274
I'm heading out early.

340
00:27:51,775 --> 00:27:52,609
See you at school.

341
00:28:16,925 --> 00:28:17,801
Hold on.

342
00:28:20,512 --> 00:28:23,139
Why are you so tense today?

343
00:28:23,223 --> 00:28:24,891
Just relax

344
00:28:25,725 --> 00:28:26,976
and don't try so hard.

345
00:28:27,060 --> 00:28:30,522
Your body tenses up when you do that.

346
00:28:59,300 --> 00:29:00,385
That's it!

347
00:29:01,177 --> 00:29:03,429
Throw the sound out like that.

348
00:29:04,848 --> 00:29:06,641
Keep your fingertips firm!

349
00:29:16,568 --> 00:29:18,903
Why did you keep checking your phone
while playing?

350
00:29:18,987 --> 00:29:21,447
It's common courtesy
to turn it off while practicing.

351
00:29:22,198 --> 00:29:23,825
Oh, sorry.

352
00:29:24,909 --> 00:29:26,744
I'm expecting an important call.

353
00:29:26,828 --> 00:29:28,204
An important call?

354
00:29:28,955 --> 00:29:30,415
What important call?

355
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:33,126
What's more important than playing piano?

356
00:29:40,258 --> 00:29:43,052
Hey, where are you going?
What about the dorm?

357
00:29:43,136 --> 00:29:44,387
I need to stop by somewhere.

358
00:29:53,438 --> 00:29:55,565
Jeez.

359
00:30:08,202 --> 00:30:09,621
Look who's calling me.

360
00:30:09,704 --> 00:30:10,872
What's the occasion?

361
00:30:10,955 --> 00:30:12,040
Are you busy?

362
00:30:12,123 --> 00:30:13,124
No.

363
00:30:13,207 --> 00:30:14,584
Can we meet up?

364
00:30:15,585 --> 00:30:16,419
Really?

365
00:30:16,502 --> 00:30:19,297
Of course, I'll be right there.

366
00:30:19,881 --> 00:30:21,591
What do you like about my playing?

367
00:30:21,674 --> 00:30:23,718
Where's this coming from?

368
00:30:23,801 --> 00:30:26,471
Why are you asking me that?

369
00:30:26,554 --> 00:30:28,890
I keep wondering

370
00:30:29,766 --> 00:30:31,476
whether I actually have talent or not.

371
00:30:31,559 --> 00:30:32,560
Hey!

372
00:30:33,269 --> 00:30:35,730
If you say that, what does that make me?

373
00:30:35,813 --> 00:30:38,816
I have zero talent, but I'm still playing.

374
00:30:40,109 --> 00:30:43,404
But you've got a really sharp ear.

375
00:30:44,322 --> 00:30:45,281
Exactly.

376
00:30:46,199 --> 00:30:48,409
I have a really sharp ear, so trust me.

377
00:30:49,118 --> 00:30:52,080
You have absolutely nothing
to worry about.

378
00:30:52,664 --> 00:30:54,457
So stop stressing out, okay?

379
00:30:56,250 --> 00:30:57,335
But still,

380
00:30:58,586 --> 00:31:01,673
what do you think are my strengths?

381
00:31:03,549 --> 00:31:04,550
I'm not sure.

382
00:31:06,135 --> 00:31:07,011
How should I put it?

383
00:31:09,847 --> 00:31:10,848
When you play,

384
00:31:12,225 --> 00:31:13,851
there's something sort of

385
00:31:14,852 --> 00:31:15,812
regal about it.

386
00:31:17,188 --> 00:31:20,316
It's aloof and restrained,

387
00:31:20,817 --> 00:31:23,152
yet manages to express everything.

388
00:31:25,863 --> 00:31:26,739
Happy now?

389
00:31:28,574 --> 00:31:30,535
Jeez, forget I even asked.

390
00:31:32,286 --> 00:31:34,539
-I need to charge my phone.
-Okay.

391
00:31:43,631 --> 00:31:45,341
RECENT HISTORY

392
00:31:45,425 --> 00:31:46,509
CLEAR WATCH HISTORY?

393
00:31:54,642 --> 00:31:55,935
Damn it.

394
00:32:07,530 --> 00:32:09,532
The phone is turned off.
You will be connected to voicemail

395
00:32:09,615 --> 00:32:11,242
-after the beep…
-What the heck?

396
00:32:13,828 --> 00:32:16,539
Where are you? Why is your phone off?

397
00:32:16,622 --> 00:32:17,707
Is something wrong…

398
00:32:21,169 --> 00:32:23,463
MR. KIM

399
00:32:23,963 --> 00:32:26,007
Who was it that you treasure most?

400
00:32:32,096 --> 00:32:34,640
Sir, what's this about?

401
00:32:34,724 --> 00:32:35,558
You curious?

402
00:32:36,184 --> 00:32:38,519
Then get over here instead of calling me.

403
00:32:42,273 --> 00:32:44,817
-The phone is turned off…
-Damn it.

404
00:32:46,486 --> 00:32:48,821
Why won't this bastard answer?

405
00:32:59,791 --> 00:33:01,667
Hey, he's here.

406
00:33:02,335 --> 00:33:03,628
You raised a good son.

407
00:33:04,837 --> 00:33:06,380
I would've just ignored you, mister.

408
00:33:08,007 --> 00:33:09,550
Hey, take it easy!

409
00:33:10,551 --> 00:33:11,677
Let go of me!

410
00:33:15,431 --> 00:33:16,265
Jeong-yo.

411
00:33:17,308 --> 00:33:18,684
Bring me 80 million won in 3 days.

412
00:33:20,269 --> 00:33:22,146
If you don't, I'll rip out his organs…

413
00:33:23,731 --> 00:33:25,608
and sell them all.

414
00:33:27,568 --> 00:33:31,572
I was going to tell you
to bring me 100 million won…

415
00:33:34,575 --> 00:33:36,577
but I can't do that to you, kid.

416
00:33:36,661 --> 00:33:38,538
Why is it 80 million all of a sudden?

417
00:33:39,997 --> 00:33:41,916
It was 20 million before!

418
00:33:43,042 --> 00:33:43,876
Twenty million?

419
00:33:45,211 --> 00:33:47,547
I'll just take out
60 million won's worth then.

420
00:33:47,630 --> 00:33:48,464
Get on your back.

421
00:33:48,548 --> 00:33:49,966
-No!
-Please!

422
00:33:51,467 --> 00:33:53,636
Please give me some more time.

423
00:33:54,512 --> 00:33:57,014
Where am I supposed to
get that money all of a sudden?

424
00:33:57,765 --> 00:34:00,184
I promise I'll try harder,
so please give me more time.

425
00:34:02,103 --> 00:34:02,979
Jeez.

426
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:06,691
Do I have to spell everything out for you?

427
00:34:06,774 --> 00:34:08,943
Use your head for a change.

428
00:34:09,026 --> 00:34:10,987
Your friend is super rich, isn't he?

429
00:34:11,696 --> 00:34:14,949
Get some settlement money from him,
or tell him you need money for a trip.

430
00:34:15,032 --> 00:34:16,534
Come up with something.

431
00:34:17,201 --> 00:34:18,995
You've got three days, Jeong-yo.

432
00:34:34,594 --> 00:34:36,304
Raise your hand for Choi Jeong-yo.

433
00:34:40,266 --> 00:34:42,101
Raise your hand for Kang Pi-o.

434
00:34:44,729 --> 00:34:47,106
I didn't expect Jeong-yo
to get more votes.

435
00:34:47,607 --> 00:34:49,650
Ji-won, why do you prefer Jeong-yo?

436
00:34:49,734 --> 00:34:52,361
I understand your concern about him.

437
00:34:53,112 --> 00:34:55,823
It might be too early to judge
based on this performance alone,

438
00:34:55,907 --> 00:34:57,408
but you can see him

439
00:34:57,491 --> 00:34:59,660
put his own creative spin on the piece.

440
00:35:00,286 --> 00:35:01,621
It looks like sheer instinct.

441
00:35:03,206 --> 00:35:05,583
Maybe he just played really well that day.

442
00:35:05,666 --> 00:35:09,003
He'll need to deliver results
at an international competition in a year.

443
00:35:09,086 --> 00:35:12,089
How are we going to train
raw talent like him that quickly?

444
00:35:13,591 --> 00:35:15,426
In that regard,

445
00:35:15,509 --> 00:35:18,346
wouldn't Pi-o have better odds
since he's well-prepared?

446
00:35:20,056 --> 00:35:22,683
But he said he won't enter
any more competitions.

447
00:35:23,309 --> 00:35:25,228
We can't wait for him to change his mind.

448
00:35:25,311 --> 00:35:28,522
If we miss out on Choi Jeong-yo,
it'll be a major loss for us.

449
00:35:35,363 --> 00:35:37,114
All right, I see your point.

450
00:35:37,698 --> 00:35:39,075
I'll think about it some more.

451
00:35:39,742 --> 00:35:40,993
That's it for today's meeting.

452
00:35:41,702 --> 00:35:43,204
-Good work.
-Thank you.

453
00:35:43,829 --> 00:35:44,956
Good job, everyone.

454
00:35:58,511 --> 00:35:59,553
Enough.

455
00:36:01,806 --> 00:36:02,682
Leave.

456
00:36:06,269 --> 00:36:07,144
Mr. Kang.

457
00:36:08,145 --> 00:36:09,897
I simply don't understand.

458
00:36:09,981 --> 00:36:13,693
She was awarded the highest prize
at the Rumina Competition.

459
00:36:13,776 --> 00:36:16,988
She's the kind of talent
everyone is fighting over.

460
00:36:17,071 --> 00:36:20,074
We bent over backward
to secure the guest soloist.

461
00:36:20,157 --> 00:36:22,201
If you dismiss her like this--

462
00:36:22,285 --> 00:36:23,160
Mr. Park.

463
00:36:23,244 --> 00:36:25,371
You majored in piano, right?

464
00:36:25,454 --> 00:36:26,414
Excuse me?

465
00:36:28,958 --> 00:36:32,670
Yet you don't know
what's wrong with how she plays?

466
00:36:33,796 --> 00:36:35,089
Now I understand

467
00:36:35,840 --> 00:36:38,384
why you never made it as a pianist.

468
00:36:44,932 --> 00:36:47,184
Let me tell you what music is, Mr. Park.

469
00:36:49,979 --> 00:36:52,064
It's a remarkable art form

470
00:36:52,148 --> 00:36:55,818
where a single genius appears,
changes everything…

471
00:36:58,070 --> 00:36:59,447
and reinvents everything.

472
00:37:00,323 --> 00:37:03,868
When I see anyone and everyone
trying their hand at it,

473
00:37:03,951 --> 00:37:06,037
I get so angry that I can't stand it.

474
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:06,996
How?

475
00:37:09,832 --> 00:37:11,834
How in the world do they have no shame?

476
00:37:31,395 --> 00:37:33,606
WHERE ARE YOU? WHEN ARE YOU GETTING BACK?
UNREAD

477
00:37:39,278 --> 00:37:40,154
Choi Jeong-yo.

478
00:37:46,369 --> 00:37:48,120
How long have you been waiting?

479
00:37:48,621 --> 00:37:51,123
I messaged you. Why didn't you check?

480
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:53,959
Oh, I…

481
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:55,961
I had to meet someone.

482
00:38:21,404 --> 00:38:23,280
Are you uncomfortable around me?

483
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:25,241
What?

484
00:38:26,117 --> 00:38:26,992
No.

485
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:30,955
Not at all. Why do you ask?
Do you feel uncomfortable?

486
00:38:33,666 --> 00:38:34,500
No.

487
00:38:37,795 --> 00:38:39,213
I'm going to wash up now.

488
00:38:39,296 --> 00:38:40,172
Okay.

489
00:39:16,709 --> 00:39:17,626
You go ahead.

490
00:39:32,766 --> 00:39:33,601
Yes?

491
00:39:37,396 --> 00:39:38,439
Jeong-yo.

492
00:39:39,315 --> 00:39:40,483
What brings you here?

493
00:39:42,985 --> 00:39:43,944
Ms. Yoon.

494
00:39:45,196 --> 00:39:46,864
Please save my dad.

495
00:39:48,199 --> 00:39:49,033
What?

496
00:40:17,686 --> 00:40:21,232
The maximum amount we can offer

497
00:40:21,315 --> 00:40:22,608
is ten million won.

498
00:40:23,442 --> 00:40:25,903
Why are you talking crap so politely,
pretty lady?

499
00:40:27,404 --> 00:40:28,405
Can't you read Korean?

500
00:40:28,489 --> 00:40:29,990
It's all written there.

501
00:40:30,491 --> 00:40:32,535
The annual interest rate is 414%.

502
00:40:33,786 --> 00:40:36,330
I guess math isn't your forte.

503
00:40:37,081 --> 00:40:38,415
If the annual rate is 414%,

504
00:40:38,499 --> 00:40:41,168
then it's 16.56 million won,
not 80 million.

505
00:40:43,254 --> 00:40:44,296
Really?

506
00:40:45,256 --> 00:40:48,217
Ms. Lee, please summarize it for him.

507
00:40:48,801 --> 00:40:51,804
Hello, I'm Attorney Lee Yun-a
with Hankook Group's legal team.

508
00:40:52,388 --> 00:40:54,390
Before we discuss this case…

509
00:40:54,890 --> 00:40:56,642
Mr. Kim Se-jin,

510
00:40:56,725 --> 00:40:58,894
you registered Happy Loan
as a lending company

511
00:40:58,978 --> 00:41:02,064
with the legally permitted
maximum interest rate of 20%.

512
00:41:02,147 --> 00:41:04,108
But the actual contract terms differ--

513
00:41:04,191 --> 00:41:05,192
Hey!

514
00:41:06,402 --> 00:41:08,821
That's enough. I get it.

515
00:41:12,032 --> 00:41:12,866
Damn it.

516
00:41:16,036 --> 00:41:18,455
Guys, let's go have some jjajangmyeon.

517
00:41:25,296 --> 00:41:26,171
Hey, Jeong-yo.

518
00:41:28,299 --> 00:41:30,801
It's money that makes art, not people.

519
00:41:41,437 --> 00:41:43,147
-Don't worry, ma'am.
-Okay.

520
00:41:43,230 --> 00:41:45,232
We'll call you
when the documents are ready.

521
00:41:45,316 --> 00:41:47,026
I'm not worried. I trust you.

522
00:41:48,277 --> 00:41:49,236
Good work today.

523
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,362
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

524
00:41:51,196 --> 00:41:52,114
Let's go.

525
00:41:53,741 --> 00:41:54,700
Thank you.

526
00:41:55,451 --> 00:41:57,161
-I'll earn the money somehow--
-Good.

527
00:41:57,244 --> 00:41:58,245
Pay me back.

528
00:41:58,787 --> 00:42:02,207
I'll assume it'll take you
ten years to pay it back,

529
00:42:02,291 --> 00:42:03,542
so forget about it for now.

530
00:42:04,335 --> 00:42:07,630
Just buy me a meal occasionally
to cover the interest.

531
00:42:14,428 --> 00:42:17,097
You've been through so much, Mr. Choi.

532
00:42:17,973 --> 00:42:20,017
You probably haven't been eating well.

533
00:42:20,100 --> 00:42:21,477
Shall we go eat?

534
00:42:25,564 --> 00:42:26,482
Mr. Choi.

535
00:42:33,364 --> 00:42:36,450
I ended up giving your son
a scholarship at our school

536
00:42:36,533 --> 00:42:38,827
without asking for your permission.

537
00:42:39,620 --> 00:42:42,581
Jeong-yo is exceptionally talented.

538
00:42:43,499 --> 00:42:45,959
How did you raise such an amazing son?

539
00:42:47,002 --> 00:42:51,131
I'd like to thank you
for not letting him give up on music

540
00:42:51,215 --> 00:42:52,466
despite all the hardship.

541
00:42:53,258 --> 00:42:54,134
This kid

542
00:42:55,344 --> 00:42:56,637
isn't my son.

543
00:43:04,895 --> 00:43:07,064
What does that even matter now?

544
00:43:10,442 --> 00:43:12,945
Neither of us had anyone to rely on.

545
00:43:13,987 --> 00:43:16,365
Have I ever been a burden to you, Dad?

546
00:43:16,448 --> 00:43:18,742
-If anything, I've been--
-It was bad enough

547
00:43:18,826 --> 00:43:20,452
being tricked into raising a kid

548
00:43:21,870 --> 00:43:23,956
who wasn't even mine for ten years.

549
00:43:25,249 --> 00:43:27,626
You expect me to keep you around
like you're my son?

550
00:43:41,598 --> 00:43:42,558
I…

551
00:43:43,726 --> 00:43:44,810
can't stand you.

552
00:43:46,145 --> 00:43:47,312
Whenever I look at you,

553
00:43:48,063 --> 00:43:51,525
I want to drag your mom
out of her grave and ask her why.

554
00:43:52,151 --> 00:43:55,112
Just looking at you drives me insane.

555
00:43:56,238 --> 00:43:59,783
You should've had the decency
to get out of my life!

556
00:44:01,660 --> 00:44:02,619
But…

557
00:44:03,454 --> 00:44:04,413
But still…

558
00:44:09,835 --> 00:44:11,253
Things were good between us.

559
00:44:16,884 --> 00:44:20,095
It was good
when you thought I was your son.

560
00:44:39,907 --> 00:44:40,741
Wait…

561
00:44:44,620 --> 00:44:46,079
Jeong-yo.

562
00:45:12,940 --> 00:45:13,774
What?

563
00:45:14,358 --> 00:45:15,317
I know.

564
00:45:16,735 --> 00:45:18,237
You must be disappointed.

565
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:19,988
But what can I do?

566
00:45:20,072 --> 00:45:21,573
I'm the head of this company,

567
00:45:21,657 --> 00:45:24,993
and I have to be objective
for the sake of my employees.

568
00:45:25,953 --> 00:45:27,913
Can't you be a little understanding?

569
00:45:27,996 --> 00:45:32,125
You couldn't even spare my son
a minute to figure things out

570
00:45:33,085 --> 00:45:34,837
and decided to switch over
to Choi Jeong-yo?

571
00:45:36,213 --> 00:45:38,674
Switch over? What do you mean?

572
00:45:39,758 --> 00:45:41,343
It's not like we're
terminating our contract.

573
00:45:42,010 --> 00:45:44,346
Just look at it as a win-win.

574
00:45:44,847 --> 00:45:46,598
They're close friends,

575
00:45:46,682 --> 00:45:50,018
and being in the same agency
makes it easier to work on projects.

576
00:45:50,102 --> 00:45:51,645
There are lots of advantages.

577
00:45:55,858 --> 00:45:58,235
Since when is an agency
trying to sign an artist

578
00:45:58,318 --> 00:45:59,945
grounds for such a harsh comment?

579
00:46:00,028 --> 00:46:01,405
I don't quite get it.

580
00:46:05,158 --> 00:46:08,161
Look, I'm only asking you to understand
because we're friends.

581
00:46:08,245 --> 00:46:11,164
I don't need your permission to do this.

582
00:46:11,915 --> 00:46:12,749
Fine.

583
00:46:14,209 --> 00:46:15,460
If that's how you feel…

584
00:46:17,462 --> 00:46:18,463
let's part ways.

585
00:46:19,214 --> 00:46:20,215
Hey.

586
00:46:20,757 --> 00:46:23,343
Why are you being so drastic?

587
00:46:26,263 --> 00:46:28,974
I can't accommodate you and Pi-o
every single time.

588
00:46:29,558 --> 00:46:31,894
That's why I'm saying we should part ways.

589
00:46:32,644 --> 00:46:33,604
However…

590
00:46:35,814 --> 00:46:37,566
I want to make one thing clear.

591
00:46:39,651 --> 00:46:41,278
You should know

592
00:46:42,029 --> 00:46:44,740
that artists hate feeling like
they're just one of many.

593
00:46:45,449 --> 00:46:47,200
They'd rather walk away.

594
00:46:47,284 --> 00:46:49,286
How can you run an agency

595
00:46:50,162 --> 00:46:52,915
without even understanding that?

596
00:47:14,478 --> 00:47:17,272
Get in. I need to talk to you.

597
00:47:17,356 --> 00:47:18,941
I've got nothing to say.

598
00:47:19,024 --> 00:47:20,609
I'm not telling you to compete.

599
00:47:20,692 --> 00:47:22,319
It's important, so get in.

600
00:47:29,618 --> 00:47:30,869
How's living on your own?

601
00:47:31,620 --> 00:47:32,454
Do you like it?

602
00:47:34,623 --> 00:47:36,249
Is that what you wanted to say?

603
00:47:37,084 --> 00:47:38,001
No.

604
00:47:39,002 --> 00:47:40,128
It's not that.

605
00:47:41,129 --> 00:47:42,547
What do you want to tell me?

606
00:47:43,090 --> 00:47:44,383
Just say it.

607
00:47:44,466 --> 00:47:45,801
Eden brought up

608
00:47:45,884 --> 00:47:48,762
terminating your contract
if you won't enter competitions.

609
00:47:48,845 --> 00:47:50,347
They said they'll sign

610
00:47:51,473 --> 00:47:52,683
Choi Jeong-yo instead.

611
00:47:53,558 --> 00:47:55,310
So I told them to go ahead.

612
00:47:55,811 --> 00:47:57,229
Good call, right?

613
00:48:19,209 --> 00:48:20,711
CHOI JEONG-YO

614
00:48:48,780 --> 00:48:50,323
ROOM 424
CHOI JEONG-YO

615
00:48:50,407 --> 00:48:54,494
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

616
00:49:02,753 --> 00:49:03,754
Did you call yesterday?

617
00:49:04,588 --> 00:49:07,007
Sorry. I went back home.

618
00:49:11,511 --> 00:49:12,888
-Come on, what is it?
-Huh?

619
00:49:14,014 --> 00:49:14,931
Oh, I…

620
00:49:15,974 --> 00:49:17,642
I called because you didn't show up.

621
00:49:18,435 --> 00:49:19,561
Let's get something to drink.

622
00:49:28,862 --> 00:49:29,696
Thank you.

623
00:49:30,322 --> 00:49:32,240
What made you go back home?

624
00:49:33,742 --> 00:49:35,786
-Well--
-What are you guys doing here?

625
00:49:38,663 --> 00:49:42,167
What kind of fun
are you plotting without me?

626
00:49:43,293 --> 00:49:44,920
We're not plotting anything.

627
00:49:45,003 --> 00:49:46,254
We were talking about practice.

628
00:49:47,756 --> 00:49:48,673
Practice?

629
00:49:49,549 --> 00:49:51,635
Are you guys working together?

630
00:49:51,718 --> 00:49:53,929
We're playing each other's
concerto accompaniments.

631
00:49:54,012 --> 00:49:55,222
Really?

632
00:49:57,599 --> 00:49:59,601
Hey, Jeong-yo.

633
00:49:59,684 --> 00:50:02,187
You never mentioned this
when you played for me.

634
00:50:04,940 --> 00:50:06,316
Can I come watch?

635
00:50:07,150 --> 00:50:08,193
No.

636
00:50:08,276 --> 00:50:11,655
Come on.
I'll just watch and stay out of the way!

637
00:50:15,659 --> 00:50:17,160
I'm so excited.

638
00:50:17,244 --> 00:50:18,286
Can I begin?

639
00:50:19,496 --> 00:50:20,330
Okay.

640
00:51:31,067 --> 00:51:34,112
What do you think about when you play?

641
00:51:34,196 --> 00:51:35,572
Nothing, really.

642
00:51:36,781 --> 00:51:37,616
I'm so jealous.

643
00:51:38,867 --> 00:51:40,744
Maybe I think too much.

644
00:51:40,827 --> 00:51:41,661
Are you tired?

645
00:51:42,412 --> 00:51:44,122
You don't look so good.

646
00:51:44,206 --> 00:51:46,583
-What?
-Oh, really?

647
00:51:46,666 --> 00:51:47,751
Yeah.

648
00:51:48,251 --> 00:51:50,420
Then can you walk Jae-in to the bus stop?

649
00:51:50,921 --> 00:51:51,755
What?

650
00:51:52,255 --> 00:51:53,798
Hey, don't be silly.

651
00:51:53,882 --> 00:51:55,175
Just go home, you two.

652
00:51:55,258 --> 00:51:56,384
No, you…

653
00:51:56,468 --> 00:51:57,594
Walk her there, okay?

654
00:51:57,677 --> 00:51:58,511
But…

655
00:52:00,972 --> 00:52:02,098
See you!

656
00:52:31,795 --> 00:52:33,588
Take your temperature when you get home.

657
00:52:33,672 --> 00:52:35,173
You were out for a long time…

658
00:52:38,134 --> 00:52:39,094
Hello, Ms. Yoon.

659
00:52:39,761 --> 00:52:41,471
Hi, can you talk?

660
00:52:42,138 --> 00:52:43,265
Yes, go ahead.

661
00:52:44,182 --> 00:52:46,101
It's time for you to pay up.

662
00:52:47,102 --> 00:52:48,103
Sorry?

663
00:52:54,150 --> 00:52:55,068
Hey, Pi-o.

664
00:52:56,945 --> 00:52:57,779
Yeah?

665
00:52:58,947 --> 00:53:01,116
Where are we practicing today?

666
00:53:02,284 --> 00:53:05,578
I've got some pieces to work on by myself,
so let's practice separately today.

667
00:53:07,038 --> 00:53:08,540
-Okay.
-See you tomorrow.

668
00:53:11,376 --> 00:53:12,210
Bye.

669
00:54:46,471 --> 00:54:49,599
You have such a great eye, as always.

670
00:54:50,100 --> 00:54:52,352
Choi Jeong-yo is really something, right?

671
00:54:52,977 --> 00:54:53,895
Yes.

672
00:54:55,313 --> 00:54:57,941
I want him to perform my concerto.

673
00:56:04,716 --> 00:56:06,593
-Encore!
-Encore!

674
00:56:06,676 --> 00:56:07,927
Encore!

675
00:56:08,511 --> 00:56:09,471
Encore!

676
00:56:15,768 --> 00:56:17,395
I was hoping for an encore,

677
00:56:17,479 --> 00:56:19,939
but he got too shy and ran off.

678
00:56:21,149 --> 00:56:24,110
I'll ask Mr. Choi to play again later.

679
00:56:24,194 --> 00:56:25,820
I'm very excited for our next guest.

680
00:56:26,654 --> 00:56:30,575
Please welcome pianist Sunwoo Ye-kwon.

681
00:56:32,410 --> 00:56:34,746
-Thanks for coming. The floor is yours.
-It's my pleasure.

682
00:56:51,429 --> 00:56:52,263
Pi-o.

683
00:56:56,684 --> 00:56:57,936
So the thing is,

684
00:56:59,103 --> 00:57:01,356
I heard about this sick child
who likes music.

685
00:57:02,815 --> 00:57:05,485
Ms. Yoon asked me to play,
but when we got here,

686
00:57:05,568 --> 00:57:06,861
I realized it was your home.

687
00:57:07,820 --> 00:57:10,365
If I'd known I'd be playing here,
I wouldn't have…

688
00:57:13,284 --> 00:57:14,160
You.

689
00:57:15,203 --> 00:57:18,164
I told you to audition for the concerto.
What's taking so long?

690
00:57:19,457 --> 00:57:20,917
Are you still deciding?

691
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:21,918
I…

692
00:57:24,796 --> 00:57:26,714
I told the director I didn't want to.

693
00:57:26,798 --> 00:57:28,383
Why are you hesitating so much?

694
00:57:28,466 --> 00:57:31,970
Don't you know playing concertos
is what truly shapes a pianist?

695
00:57:33,137 --> 00:57:34,514
Stop being lazy

696
00:57:35,098 --> 00:57:36,474
and come to my office tomorrow.

697
00:57:37,308 --> 00:57:38,518
But sir…

698
00:57:41,104 --> 00:57:43,273
Let me explain. The truth is…

699
00:57:45,066 --> 00:57:46,609
Pi-o.

700
00:57:46,693 --> 00:57:47,610
Kang Pi-o!

701
00:57:52,156 --> 00:57:54,284
What does Choi Jeong-yo have that I don't?

702
00:57:54,867 --> 00:57:56,160
You know how badly

703
00:57:57,078 --> 00:57:59,289
I've wanted to perform with you!

704
00:58:00,081 --> 00:58:01,082
So why?

705
00:58:03,334 --> 00:58:05,295
Why is it Choi Jeong-yo and not me?

706
00:58:05,962 --> 00:58:08,131
Do I really have to spell it out for you?

707
00:58:08,214 --> 00:58:11,134
But you said I was good
at the Noblesse Classical Concert!

708
00:58:11,718 --> 00:58:12,677
You said you'd come

709
00:58:13,845 --> 00:58:15,513
and watch me perform again.

710
00:58:16,097 --> 00:58:20,184
The Noblesse Classical performance
wasn't good because you played well.

711
00:58:21,728 --> 00:58:24,272
Choi Jeong-yo carried that performance,

712
00:58:25,523 --> 00:58:28,526
and you were just swept up
in his raw emotion.

713
00:58:29,193 --> 00:58:31,654
He's fundamentally different from you.

714
00:58:31,738 --> 00:58:34,741
You calculate everything,
but he plays on instinct.

715
00:58:35,742 --> 00:58:37,785
You analyze the structure,

716
00:58:37,869 --> 00:58:42,248
but he pours music out of his heart
like exploding lava.

717
00:58:42,332 --> 00:58:43,916
That's why people

718
00:58:44,000 --> 00:58:47,587
find your music flawless yet boring.

719
00:58:48,630 --> 00:58:50,089
But when they listen to his,

720
00:58:50,173 --> 00:58:52,008
they're captivated even if it's imperfect.

721
00:58:53,301 --> 00:58:54,344
Something like that…

722
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,388
simply can't be taught!

723
00:58:58,681 --> 00:59:00,642
That's not true at all!

724
00:59:00,725 --> 00:59:02,352
You're wrong, Mr. Kang.

725
00:59:03,394 --> 00:59:04,687
You don't know this,

726
00:59:05,355 --> 00:59:06,856
but Pi-o carried me that day.

727
00:59:06,939 --> 00:59:08,608
I was able to play because of him,

728
00:59:08,691 --> 00:59:10,610
and my emotions ran high because of him!

729
00:59:10,693 --> 00:59:14,530
What gives you the right to compare us
when you don't know anything?

730
00:59:15,323 --> 00:59:16,157
Knock it off.

731
00:59:16,240 --> 00:59:17,909
Knock what off?

732
00:59:18,451 --> 00:59:19,952
I can feel it!

733
00:59:20,036 --> 00:59:22,538
Your raw talent is more brilliant
and extraordinary than mine!

734
00:59:23,706 --> 00:59:26,417
I find your friendship oddly amusing.

735
00:59:29,003 --> 00:59:29,879
But Pi-o…

736
00:59:31,839 --> 00:59:33,132
You see it clearly now, right?

737
00:59:34,509 --> 00:59:36,427
You know who'll be left

738
00:59:36,511 --> 00:59:38,805
broken and destroyed in this relationship.

739
00:59:49,941 --> 00:59:50,942
Pi-o.

740
01:00:13,506 --> 01:00:14,340
Pi-o.

741
01:00:15,842 --> 01:00:17,176
Leave my son alone.

742
01:00:19,470 --> 01:00:22,014
-I'm really sorry, but--
-Don't you get it?

743
01:00:22,974 --> 01:00:24,100
This is all your fault.

744
01:00:25,017 --> 01:00:25,893
I'm warning you.

745
01:00:26,644 --> 01:00:27,979
Don't ever approach Pi-o again.

746
01:00:28,062 --> 01:00:29,564
If I see you one more time…

747
01:00:31,315 --> 01:00:33,192
I'll make you regret it. Understand?

748
01:01:04,599 --> 01:01:05,558
Pi-o.

749
01:01:09,687 --> 01:01:10,521
Pi-o?

750
01:01:17,236 --> 01:01:18,362
Pi-o.

751
01:01:23,659 --> 01:01:24,869
Pi-o!

752
01:01:36,214 --> 01:01:37,924
Pi-o!

753
01:01:38,007 --> 01:01:40,635
Pi-o, wake up! Pi-o!

754
01:01:42,053 --> 01:01:43,054
Pi-o.

755
01:01:43,846 --> 01:01:46,724
SPECIAL THANKS TO SUNWOO YE-KWON
FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

756
01:02:07,662 --> 01:02:09,831
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

757
01:02:09,914 --> 01:02:12,375
Why do you say I'll never make it?

758
01:02:13,042 --> 01:02:14,961
Because you have no talent.

759
01:02:15,044 --> 01:02:16,295
I'm not a genius.

760
01:02:16,379 --> 01:02:18,840
If I don't prove myself on stage,
who'll listen to me play?

761
01:02:19,757 --> 01:02:21,425
I want to ask you

762
01:02:21,509 --> 01:02:23,010
to enter the same competition.

763
01:02:23,636 --> 01:02:25,137
What's wrong with your pinky finger?

764
01:02:25,638 --> 01:02:27,765
Why did he have us play the same piece?

765
01:02:27,849 --> 01:02:29,016
You're not yourself right now.

766
01:02:29,100 --> 01:02:30,476
Knock it off! Stop!

767
01:02:30,560 --> 01:02:32,770
Do you want to get kicked out
before you even compete?

768
01:02:33,646 --> 01:02:34,981
If I don't win the competition,

769
01:02:35,815 --> 01:02:37,316
I'm going to quit the piano.

770
01:02:38,317 --> 01:02:43,322
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

